course: dictionary
lesson: 6639
title: Nozzles: where things come out
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A nozzle is the narrow tube or spout at the end of a hose, pipe or can. It controls how a liquid or gas comes out. Think of the spray from a garden hose: the nozzle decides whether it comes out as a thin jet or a fine mist.
explain: Use the context to work out new words. «A vacuum cleaner does not really suck: its fan throws air out of the back, the pressure inside drops, and the outside air rushes in at the nozzle, carrying the crumbs with it.» Air and crumbs rush in through an opening, so the nozzle is the opening where they come in.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try "the outside air rushes in at the narrow tube, carrying the crumbs with it." It still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Spiders have nozzles too. «Real spiders make silk ... and pull it out through little nozzles called spinnerets at the back end.» So a spinneret is a spider's nozzle for silk, and the word nozzle is used in science as well as in everyday life.
fact: A nozzle is a narrow tube or spout at the end of a hose, pipe or can.
fact: A nozzle controls how a liquid or gas comes out.
fact: «A narrow nozzle makes water come out faster and further.»
fact: Spiders make silk through «little nozzles called spinnerets» at the back end of their bodies.
fact: Safety: never point a hose or spray nozzle at someone's face, and do not look into a spray nozzle.
exercise: «The outside air rushes in at the nozzle, carrying the crumbs with it.» What is the nozzle here? | *A narrow opening where the air and crumbs come in | A bag full of crumbs | A loud noise from the fan | A light that switches on
exercise: «Real spiders make silk ... pull it out through little nozzles called spinnerets.» What comes out of the spinnerets? | Heat | *Silk | Dust | Water
exercise: Dad twists the nozzle on the garden hose so the water comes out as a fine spray. What is the nozzle for? | To hold the hose up | To stop the garden growing | *To control how the water comes out | To make the hose longer
test: What does a narrow nozzle do to water? | Makes it stay in the hose | Makes it turn to dust | *Makes it come out faster and further | Makes it colder
test: Why should you never point a spray nozzle at someone's face? | It makes a rainbow | It makes them grow taller | It makes the nozzle heavier | *It could hurt them
exam: The word nozzle means: | A kind of spider | A loud noise made by a fan | A large tank that holds petrol | *A narrow tube or spout that controls how a liquid or gas comes out
